orge Herbert was an English poet, orator, and priest of the Church of England. His poetry is associated with the writings of the metaphysical poets, and he is recognised as "one of the foremost British devotional lyricists." He was born in Wales into an artistic and wealthy family and largely raised in England. He received a good education that led to his admission to Trinity College, Cambridge, in 1609.

He enrolled intending to become a priest, but became the University's Public Orator and attracted the attention of King James I. George Herbert was a religious figures from Montgomery (1593-04-03, Montgomery–1633-03-01). Holds notable historical significance, documented across 0 language editions of Wikipedia.", "newValue": "George Herbert (1593–1633) stands as a pivotal figure in early 17th-century English literature, renowned for his devotional lyric poetry that profoundly influenced the metaphysical school and the Anglican tradition. Born into a prominent Anglo-Welsh artistic and aristocratic family, including his brother Edward Herbert, 1st Baron Herbert of Cherbury, his works offer an intricate exploration of faith, doubt, and the spiritual journey, cementing his reputation as 'one of the foremost British devotional lyricists.' His concise yet complex verse, characterized by its intellectual rigor and emotional depth, continues to resonate within both literary and theological circles.

